01:03:09,473 --> 01:03:15,473
Birth is a 2004 American psychological drama film
co-written and directed by Jonathan Glazer.

13
01:08:25,263 --> 01:08:31,263
The film stars Nicole Kidman, Lauren Bacall, Cameron Bright, Danny Huston,
Arliss Howard, Peter Stormare, Ted Levine, and Anne Heche.

14
01:13:41,052 --> 01:13:47,052
Its plot follows a woman who becomes convinced that her deceased
husband Sean is reincarnated as a ten-year-old boy.

15
01:18:56,842 --> 01:19:02,842
Distributed by New Line Cinema, Birth premiered in competition at the 61st Venice International Film
Festival, polarizing critics upon its release and grossing $23.9 million on a budget of $20 million.

16
01:24:12,631 --> 01:24:18,631
Kidman was nominated for a Golden Globe Award for Best Actress
in a Motion Picture – Drama for her performance.

17
01:29:28,421 --> 01:29:34,421
The film explores themes of infidelity, new york city,
opera, loss of loved one, love letter.

18
01:34:44,210 --> 01:34:50,210
The tone is emotional and mind_bending.
